# interplay_memlive_readonly_flip: Bit 31 of a live shared buffer's leaf flipped both ways. A buffer made over a writable leaf takes fills after the leaf turns read-only: its mapping or backing was made writable. Discarded (63) and listed again it is bound read-only: in the map setup the mapping of a range with a read-only page is read-only and in the service the backing carries the leaves' read-only bit, and the GPU's fill is dropped without a fault; the blocks setup's host task maps it writable (and keeps its old mapping), so fills land. The leaf made writable again changes nothing until another 63.
